    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-38862",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
